    "turns": [
        {
            "role": "A",
            "text": "Behind the technical name Gradient Boosting, what intuitive problem were researchers confronting?",
            "sourceIds": [],
            "claimIds": [],
            "contentOrigin": "editorial-hook"
        },
        {
            "role": "B",
            "text": "Boosting was often described through classification-specific reweighting rules. Friedman recast it as stage-wise function optimization, allowing the same idea to minimize many differentiable loss functions.",
            "sourceIds": ["source-2001-gradient-boosting-primary", "source-benchcouncil-ai100-catalog"],
            "claimIds": ["claim-2001-gradient-boosting-membership", "claim-2001-gradient-boosting-description"],
            "contentOrigin": "commentarySections.historical-background"
        },
        {
            "role": "A",
            "text": "That sounds like a promising direction. What mechanism actually makes it work?",
            "sourceIds": [],
            "claimIds": [],
            "contentOrigin": "editorial"
        },
        {
            "role": "B",
            "text": "Each new weak learner fits the negative gradient, or pseudo-residual, of the current model’s loss. Adding that learner moves the ensemble toward lower loss in function space.",
            "sourceIds": ["source-2001-gradient-boosting-primary"],
            "claimIds": ["claim-2001-gradient-boosting-membership", "claim-2001-gradient-boosting-description"],
            "contentOrigin": "commentarySections.core-idea"
        },
        {
            "role": "A",
            "text": "Why did the idea outlive one paper or experiment? What did later researchers actually inherit?",
            "sourceIds": [],
            "claimIds": [],
            "contentOrigin": "editorial"
        },
        {
            "role": "B",
            "text": "Experts generally treat gradient boosting as the unifying optimization view behind modern boosted-tree systems. It became a dominant approach for structured data and enabled specialized implementations such as XGBoost and LightGBM.",
            "sourceIds": ["source-2001-gradient-boosting-primary", "source-2001-gradient-boosting-secondary"],
            "claimIds": ["claim-2001-gradient-boosting-membership", "claim-2001-gradient-boosting-description"],
            "contentOrigin": "commentarySections.long-term-legacy"
        },
        {
            "role": "SUMMARY",
            "text": "Gradient Boosting mattered not only as a result, but as a method that later researchers could test, adapt, and extend.",
            "sourceIds": [
                "source-2001-gradient-boosting-primary",
                "source-2001-gradient-boosting-secondary",
                "source-benchcouncil-ai100-catalog",
                "source-2001-gradient-boosting-portrait"
            ],
